cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ElecTrace in research, cite the archived software release
  and the external electronic-structure tools used in your workflow.
title: "ElecTrace: time-resolved electronic-topology tracking"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ellis
    given-names: Austin
version: 0.1.0a5
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  ElecTrace is a research-software framework for tracking electronic-topology
  evidence across ordered periodic structures, with an initial focus on VASP NEB
  images and static pressure series.
keywords:
  - electronic structure
  - chemical bonding
  - QTAIM
  - electron localization function
  - Bader charge
  - nudged elastic band
  - periodic systems
repository-code: "https://github.com/Austin243/ElecTrace"
